# Internal-only working notes and Claude Code session state — not meant for a
# public repo. docs-reference/ in particular held a full internal security
# review of the LIVE production platforms (foundation/foundation-mobile),
# removed 2026-09-02 after this repo went public.
docs-reference/
HANDOFF.md
.claude/

# Firebase — contain live API keys; injected at build time from CI secret / local keychain
ios/FoundationMobile/GoogleService-Info.plist
ios/FoundationMobile/GoogleService-Info-staging.plist
# Task A2 quarantined the old ios/ tree to legacy-ios-shell/ (git mv) without
# updating these paths — the files above are now dead entries and these two
# are what's actually needed. Kept both: the old paths are harmless if the
# B-track port later recreates a similarly-named target under the new ios/.
legacy-ios-shell/FoundationMobile/GoogleService-Info.plist
legacy-ios-shell/FoundationMobile/GoogleService-Info-staging.plist
# Task A2's subtree import brought in Rarimo's own GoogleService-Info.plist
# at this path, tracked (it's their own already-public Firebase config, not
# a leak) - untracked here pre-emptively because a future B-track task WILL
# overwrite this file's content with Foundation's real foundation-next-app
# credentials, and a plain `git add`/commit at that point would otherwise
# push a real secret straight into this now-public repo. If B-track renames
# this file/path during rebrand, add the new path here too.
ios/Rarime/GoogleService-Info.plist

